one day Matt is riding his skateboard  when he crashes and falls hitting his  head Matt's brain collides with his  skull stretching and tearing some of his  brain tissue Matt has sustained a  concussion concussions are also called  mild traumatic brain injuries you might  be wondering how do these types of  injuries occur normally your brain is  suspended in a cushioning liquid called  cerebral spinal fluid  this fluid allows your brain to stay put  even as your body moves but the high  force impacts associated with a  concussion overwhelm the protection  provided by this special fluid think  about the brain as a very fast computer  that runs your body just like computers  the brain needs a well controlled and  stable environment the blood-brain  barrier creates and maintains this  environment the blood-brain barrier is  made up of blood vessels surrounded by  astrocytes and neurons this barrier is  the brain's gatekeeper and controls what  gets into or comes out of the brain to  ensure that brain cells stay happy it  also provides essential nutrients to all  brain cells when a concussion occurs  some neurons and astrocytes get  stretched and twisted most importantly  some blood vessels brake allowing  molecules that aren't supposed to be in  the brain to get inside these molecules  upset neurons and astrocytes the cells  ask for help from the rest of the body  by sending out chemical distress signals  called biomarkers researchers use  specialized lab equipment to measure  biomarkers in patients blood or saliva -  such blood biomarkers have recently been  approved by the FDA for clinical use and  hopefully doctors will be able to use  these biomarkers to diagnose concussions  however until this new blood test is  readily available doctors still need to  make a diagnosis by examining patients  and asking them as well as their family  and friends  a long list of questions about the  patient's physical cognitive and  behavioral symptoms now we know what  happens inside your brain but what does  this mean for Matt Matt's brain needs  complete rest  meaning no TV no computer time and no  strenuous activity even though he may  not be able to see the harm done to his  brain like he could with a broken arm  brain injuries are serious medical  conditions what started out as a  concussion could become a larger problem  later in life if Matt doesn't take the  appropriate time to recover  [Music]
 

